-- `Std.Rxi.Iterator.toList_eq_match` (hypothesis 2, Std.Rxi.IsAlwaysFinite α): necessary; Nat (lawful, not Rxi.IsAlwaysFinite): the equation gives length L(k) = length L(k+1) + 1 for L(k) = toList of the iterator at some k, an infinite descent (no_descent)
theorem Rxi.Iterator.toList_eq_match.h2 : ¬ drop0% Std.Rxi.Iterator.toList_eq_match 2 := fun h =>
  no_descent (fun k => (⟨⟨some k⟩⟩ : Iter (α := Rxi.Iterator Nat) Nat).toList) fun k => by
    have := congrArg List.length (h (α := Nat) (it := ⟨⟨some k⟩⟩))
    simpa using this

